Spec: Suspended owned Windows runtime processes

Purpose:
  Launch verified noninteractive runtimes inside a kill-on-close Job before any child code executes.

Owns:
  ./LinkGate.Processes.csproj
  ./OwnedProcess.cs

Must:
  Hold and hash the selected executable, create suspended and assign the Job before resuming.
  Inherit only explicit standard handles, use direct Win32 argument quoting and keep private output in a new protected directory.
  Optional standard input comes from an explicitly selected non-linked file, never secret command-line interpolation.
  Hold actual process and Job handles through lifetime; stop only this Job and never enumerate or kill by name or port.
  Close failed suspended processes, threads, attributes, handles and locks on every startup failure.
